              "Short": "ה-00860051",
              "StudyContentDescription": "Calculus of variations, Hamilton’s principle, and classical theory of\r\nplates. Plates with shallow curvature. Modelling constraints using\r\nLagrange’s multipliers. Unsteady linear potential flow aerodynamics and\r\ncavity acoustics in response to flexible wall motion. Flutter,\r\ndivergence, and buckling of elastic plates.\r\n\r\n  Learning Outcomes:\r\n\t\r\nAfter completing the course students will be able to:\r\n1.\tDerive equations of motions and boundary conditions of thin-shell\r\nstructures using variational methods.\r\n2.\tAnalyze problems that include interaction between elastic plates,\r\nfreestream flow, and acoustic pressure in terms of stability (flutter,\r\ndivergence, and buckling) and transient response.\r\n3.\tImplement Ritz methods to obtain numerical solutions and perform\r\nstability and transient analyses in generalized coordinates.",
